{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"frontend","type":"text","text":"# 1. FRONTEND — React / TypeScript\n\nUser opens Retail Stock screen.\n\nReact calls:\n`GET http://localhost:8000/api/products`\n\n```tsx\nconst [products, setProducts] = useState([]);\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  fetch(\"http://localhost:8000/api/products\")\n    .then(res => res.json())\n    .then(data => setProducts(data));\n}, []);\n```\n\nFrontend responsibility:\n- Display data\n- Collect user input\n- Call backend APIs\n- Handle loading/error/success\n\nReact should NOT directly access PostgreSQL.","x":0,"y":0,"width":500,"height":600,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"request","type":"text","text":"# 2. HTTP REQUEST\n\nReact sends:\n`GET /api/products`\n\nCommon methods:\n- GET → Read\n- POST → Create\n- PUT/PATCH → Update\n- DELETE → Delete\n\nExample:\n\n```ts\nfetch(\"http://localhost:8000/api/stock/in\", {\n  method: \"POST\",\n  headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" },\n  body: JSON.stringify({\n    product_id: 101,\n    warehouse_id: \"WH-001\",\n    quantity: 20\n  })\n});\n```","x":600,"y":0,"width":500,"height":600,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fastapi","type":"text","text":"# 3. BACKEND — Python FastAPI\n\nFastAPI receives the request.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.get(\"/api/products\")\ndef get_products():\n    return [\n        {\"id\": 101, \"name\": \"T-Shirt\", \"stock\": 25},\n        {\"id\": 102, \"name\": \"Jeans\", \"stock\": 12}\n    ]\n```\n\nFlow:\nReact → HTTP request → FastAPI route → Python function → JSON response","x":1200,"y":0,"width":500,"height":600,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"service","type":"text","text":"# 4. SERVICE / BUSINESS LOGIC\n\nKeep business rules separate from the API route.\n\n```python\n# services/product_service.py\n\ndef get_products():\n    return product_repository.get_all()\n```\n\nRoute:\n```python\n@app.get(\"/api/products\")\ndef get_products():\n    return product_service.get_products()\n```\n\nRouter = HTTP communication\nService = business logic\nRepository = database access","x":1800,"y":0,"width":500,"height":600,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"database","type":"text","text":"# 5. DATABASE\n\nRepository communicates with PostgreSQL.\n\nRetail tables may include:\n- products\n- stock\n- warehouses\n- stock_movements\n\nExample:\n```python\ndef get_all():\n    return db.query(\"SELECT * FROM products\")\n```\n\nReact never talks directly to the database.\n\nReact → FastAPI → Service → Repository → PostgreSQL","x":2400,"y":0,"width":500,"height":600,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"response","type":"text","text":"# 6. JSON RESPONSE\n\nFastAPI returns JSON.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": 101, \"name\": \"T-Shirt\", \"stock\": 25},\n  {\"id\": 102, \"name\": \"Jeans\", \"stock\": 12}\n]\n```\n\nHTTP status:\n`200 OK`\n\nReact receives the JSON and updates state.","x":3000,"y":0,"width":500,"height":600,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"stock","type":"text","text":"# RETAIL EXAMPLE — STOCK IN\n\nUser receives 20 T-Shirts into warehouse WH-001.\n\nFrontend sends:\n`POST /api/stock/in`\n\nRequest:\n```json\n{\n  \"product_id\": 101,\n  \"warehouse_id\": \"WH-001\",\n  \"quantity\": 20\n}\n```\n\nFastAPI:\n```python\n@app.post(\"/api/stock/in\")\ndef stock_in(request: StockInRequest):\n    return stock_service.stock_in(request)\n```\n\nService:\n- Validate product\n- Validate warehouse\n- Increase stock\n- Create stock movement\n\nDatabase:\n- Update `stock`\n- Insert `stock_movements`\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\"message\":\"Stock added successfully\",\"new_stock\":45}\n```","x":0,"y":700,"width":700,"height":700,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"layers","type":"text","text":"# BACKEND LAYERS\n\n### API / Router\nHandles HTTP.\n\n### Service\nHandles Retail business rules.\n\n### Repository\nHandles database operations.\n\n### PostgreSQL\nStores data.\n\nSimple rule:\n\nRouter = How does the client communicate?\n\nService = What should the application do?\n\nRepository = How do we store/retrieve it?\n\nDatabase = Where is the data stored?","x":800,"y":700,"width":600,"height":700,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"frontend_structure","type":"text","text":"# REACT PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\n```text\nsrc/\n├── pages/\n│   └── StockPage.tsx\n├── components/\n│   └── StockTable.tsx\n├── services/\n│   └── stockApi.ts\n└── types/\n    └── stock.ts\n```\n\nAPI service:\n```ts\nexport async function getProducts() {\n  const response = await fetch(\"http://localhost:8000/api/products\");\n  return response.json();\n}\n```\n\nKeep API calls in an API/service layer instead of putting every fetch directly in UI components.","x":1500,"y":750,"width":650,"height":650,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"backend_structure","type":"text","text":"# FASTAPI PROJECT STRUCTURE\n\n```text\napp/\n├── main.py\n├── routers/\n│   └── stock.py\n├── services/\n│   └── stock_service.py\n├── repositories/\n│   └── stock_repository.py\n├── models/\n│   └── stock.py\n└── database/\n    └── connection.py\n```\n\nRequest:\nmain.py → router → service → repository → PostgreSQL\n\nResponse:\nPostgreSQL → repository → service → router → JSON → React","x":2250,"y":750,"width":600,"height":650,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"cors","type":"text","text":"# CORS\n\nDuring local development:\n\nFrontend: `localhost:5173`\nBackend: `localhost:8000`\n\nThese are different origins.\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware\n\napp.add_middleware(\n    CORSMiddleware,\n    allow_origins=[\"http://localhost:5173\"],\n    allow_credentials=True,\n    allow_methods=[\"*\"],\n    allow_headers=[\"*\"]\n)\n```\n\nWithout correct CORS configuration, the browser can block the request.","x":2950,"y":750,"width":600,"height":500,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"errors","type":"text","text":"# HTTP ERROR FLOW\n\n200 → Success\n201 → Created\n400 → Bad request\n401 → Not authenticated\n403 → Not allowed\n404 → Not found\n500 → Backend/server error\n\nReact should handle:\nLoading → Success\n\nor\n\nLoading → Error","x":3650,"y":700,"width":500,"height":500,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"mental","type":"text","text":"# SIMPLE MENTAL MODEL\n\nFor every Retail feature ask:\n\n1. What does the user do?\n2. What API is required?\n3. What data does React send?\n4. Which FastAPI route receives it?\n5. What business logic happens?\n6. Which database tables change?\n7. What JSON response comes back?\n8. What does React do with it?\n\n# REMEMBER\n\nUI → API → Backend Logic → Database → Backend → API → UI","x":4300,"y":0,"width":700,"height":850,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ui","type":"text","text":"# 7. REACT UI\n\nReact stores the response:\n\n```tsx\nsetProducts(data);\n```\n\nThen renders:\n\n```tsx\n{products.map(product => (\n  <div key={product.id}>\n    <h3>{product.name}</h3>\n    <p>Stock: {product.stock}</p>\n  </div>\n))}\n```\n\nUser sees the latest stock information.","x":3600,"y":-20,"width":500,"height":500,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a419e4cc69a83477","x":1620,"y":-1300,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"frontend"},
		{"id":"527ef13c1aaf85a5","x":2040,"y":-1300,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"backend"},
		{"id":"9ea8e9ef1055d8c3","x":2040,"y":-1153,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"business logic run"},
		{"id":"92ec07a8c2e3c212","x":2483,"y":-1301,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"frontend"},
		{"id":"ae0bd4166d28fc48","x":2804,"y":-1303,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"render"},
		{"id":"fullflow","type":"text","text":"# COMPLETE K RUISE RETAIL API FLOW\n\n```text\nRETAIL USER\n    ↓\nREACT FRONTEND\n    ↓ HTTP + JSON\nFASTAPI ROUTER\n    ↓\nSERVICE / BUSINESS LOGIC\n    ↓\nREPOSITORY\n    ↓\nPOSTGRESQL\n    ↓\nREPOSITORY\n    ↓\nSERVICE\n    ↓\nFASTAPI JSON RESPONSE\n    ↓\nREACT UI\n    ↓\nUSER SEES RESULT\n```\n\n## One sentence\n\n**UI → API → Backend Logic → Database → API → UI**","x":1825,"y":1600,"width":850,"height":800,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"practice","type":"text","text":"# PRACTICE TASKS\n\n### Level 1 — GET\n`GET /api/products`\nDisplay products.\n\n### Level 2 — GET by ID\n`GET /api/products/{id}`\nDisplay one product.\n\n### Level 3 — POST\n`POST /api/stock/in`\nAdd stock from React.\n\n### Level 4 — PATCH\n`PATCH /api/products/{id}`\nUpdate product.\n\n### Level 5 — DELETE\n`DELETE /api/products/{id}`\nDelete product.\n\n### Level 6 — Full Retail flow\nProduct → Warehouse → Stock In → Stock Movement → Current Stock → Dashboard\n\nLearn the request/response cycle before moving to the full flow.","x":-160,"y":1600,"width":700,"height":920,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"debug","type":"text","text":"# DEBUGGING TOOLS\n\n### Browser DevTools → Network\nCheck:\n- Request URL\n- HTTP method\n- Payload\n- Status code\n- Response\n- Duration\n\n### FastAPI Swagger\n`http://localhost:8000/docs`\n\n### Backend terminal\nCheck FastAPI logs.\n\n### DBeaver / PostgreSQL\nCheck whether the database changed.\n\n# DEBUGGING ORDER\n\n1. Browser Network\n2. API URL\n3. Swagger\n4. FastAPI logs\n5. Database\n\nThis prevents guessing where the problem is.","x":960,"y":2000,"width":650,"height":700,"color":"1"}
	],
